+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] tests/qtest: test the sun4m NVRAM kept in a drive
+
+qtest sun4m-nvram-test for the patch before, eight cases on the SS-5's
+M48T08:
+- no-image: without a drive the NVRAM gets OpenBIOS's layout and the
+  IDPROM as before.
+- blank: a blank image gets the same contents and keeps them.
+- persist: an image with a Sun PROM's contents stays as it is; a guest
+  write reaches the image, a clock register write does not; another MAC
+  address changes only the IDPROM.
+- prom-env: -prom-env writes OpenBIOS's partitions over it.
+- larger-image: a 16 KB image is accepted and its tail is left alone.
+- blockdev: with -blockdev, query-block names /machine/nvram.
+- read-only: a read-only image is loaded and not written.
+- delayed-write: a write is not in the image at once, and is 100 ms
+  later; a write followed by a system reset still reaches it.
+
+LEMU's version of the test, taken back unchanged (LEMU local branch,
+not pushed yet); the meson.build line follows sun4m-onboard-sbus-test
+here.
