+From: Ørjan Malde <red@foxi.me>
+Subject: [PATCH] hw/rtc/m48t59: back the NVRAM with a block device
+
+Add a "drive" property to isa-m48t59: the NVRAM is read from it at
+realize, and dirty bytes are written back 100 ms after the first write
+of a batch and when the VM stops. The image must match the NVRAM size.
+A read-only "persistent" property tells boards a drive is attached.
+Unlike a plain file, this honors -snapshot.
+
