+compiled Debian 7's sparc64 kernel: need_resched() tested at the top,
+the test of tlb_type against hypervisor with the be,pn to the sun4v
+branch and mov 14, %o0 in its delay slot, the call of
+touch_nmi_watchdog() and the sun4v branch's clear_bit() call. The loop
+runs at interrupt level 0: the CPU must halt there, and not with
+TIF_NEED_RESCHED set, without PSTATE.IE, at level 14 (where the later
+kernels' loop halts) or at level 15; with a tick every millisecond the
+tick must wake the CPU and the loop must run far fewer rounds than with
+idle-halt=off.
