+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] tests/qtest: test the FreeBSD idle loop on sun4u
+
+sun4u-idle-test gets FreeBSD 12's sched_idletd() layout with the cases
+of the others, run at TL 1 as FreeBSD's kernel runs (the boot PROM now
+has a trap table for TL>0 too, for the tick taken there). A new case,
+tl-up, runs each loop one trap level above where its kernel idles (TL 1,
+FreeBSD TL 2): the CPU must not halt there. The FreeBSD loop counts a
+round before it starts, as the CPU halts at its first idle call.
+
+Without the previous patch freebsd/idle fails (the loop goes on
+counting); with the FreeBSD layout halted at TL 0 only it fails too. 70
+cases.
