+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] tests/qtest: test the cs4231's pi and pmi for a short
+ buffer on sun4m
+
+short-buffer plays one buffer of 40 bytes (5 ms): the first interrupt
+must be PI alone, PMI must not come while PI is not cleared, and must
+come at once when it is. short-tail plays 800 bytes and then 40: the
+PI for the short buffer must come when the long one has played, without
+PMI, and PMI a few ms after that PI is cleared.
+
+load-on-pd loads a third buffer as soon as PD shows, without waiting
+for a PI: there must be three PIs for the three buffers and one PMI.
+short-chain loads 20 buffers of 40 bytes, each at the PI of the one
+before: they must play in their 100 ms.
+migrate saves the machine to a file while the PI of a 40 byte buffer is
+set and PMI waits behind it, loads it in a second QEMU and clears the
+PI there: PMI must still come.
+
+playback now also expects the second PI and the PMI no earlier than
+80 ms after the interrupt before them: they come when the codec has
+played the 100 ms buffer, not when the samples are taken.
+
+SunOS 4.1.4's driver needs PI and PMI in two interrupts, see the
+previous commit.
+
+Tested: all seven pass, three runs. Without the previous commit
+short-buffer fails: PI and PMI are set together (0x00408000). Against
+earlier versions of the previous commit load-on-pd fails without its PD
+change (two PIs for three buffers), migrate without its subsection (PMI
+never comes), and short-chain without the take at load (the pipe runs
+empty after the second buffer).
+
+Origin: https://github.com/hwinther/lemu/commit/0a78fc843fa16ce41fa723ceba1071a2d473a011
