diff --git a/debian/patches/wsh/0131-ui-dbus-add-display-dbus-refresh-ms-N.patch b/debian/patches/wsh/0131-ui-dbus-add-display-dbus-refresh-ms-N.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2ad510c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/wsh/0131-ui-dbus-add-display-dbus-refresh-ms-N.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,206 @@
+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] ui/dbus: add -display dbus,refresh-ms=N
+
+The D-Bus display's listeners never set an update interval, so the
+console refreshed at GUI_REFRESH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT, 30 ms: a client
+streaming a 70 Hz guest mode got at most 33 updates a second of a
+VGA's screen (the device's dirty memory is looked at once per
+refresh).
+
+refresh-ms=N (1 to 3000, a new member of DisplayDBus and a property of
+the dbus-display object) sets the interval of each client's listener
+when it registers (qemu_console_listener_set_refresh()), so the
+display refreshes that often while a client listens, and at its usual
+pace without one. 0, the default, keeps 30 ms.
+
+Tested with a guest that changes VGA text memory every few
+milliseconds and a client that counts the refreshes its updates come
+in: 33.6 a second by default, 61.6 with refresh-ms=14 and 125 with
+refresh-ms=5 under TCG on a loaded host (the timer is set from the end
+of each refresh, so the rate stays below 1000/N).
