+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] tests/qtest: test a break on a serial line of the sun4m
+ ESCC
+
+sun4m-escc-break-test sends breaks with chardev-send-break to ttya and
+ttyb of an SS-5 (null chardevs), the channels set up for 9600 baud as
+Solaris sets up its console port, and watches RR0, RR3, the vector in
+RR2 of channel B and the chip's interrupt. start-and-end: a break raises
+the external/status interrupt of channel A with the bit set; it stays
+latched past the character time while the guest doesn't service it;
+the guest's reset ends it, with the NUL in the receiver (receive named
+first) and a second interrupt, and a second reset leaves nothing
+pending. end-after-char-time: the start reset at once (as Linux does),
+the end comes after one character time. polled: with no interrupt
+enabled the line stays down and RR0 shows the break while it lasts.
+channel-b: the vector of channel B's external/status interrupt.
+channel-reset: a channel reset drops the pending interrupt. All five fail
+without the previous patch (polled because the line went up with WR15's
+break enable alone, channel-reset because the bit never went back to 0).
