++/*
++ * QTest: a break on a serial line of the sun4m ESCC
++ *
++ * A break sets the Break/Abort bit of RR0 and, with the external/status
++ * interrupt enabled, latches that interrupt. The bit must go back to 0
++ * when the break ends, with a second interrupt and the NUL character a
++ * real SCC leaves in the receiver: Solaris and SunOS enter the PROM at the
++ * end of a break on the console, and Linux waits for the end in its
++ * interrupt handler. RR3 and the vector in RR2 of channel B must name the
++ * external/status interrupt, and the guest's Reset Ext/Status Interrupts
++ * command must take it away.
++ *
++ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
++ */
++
