+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] target/sparc: read back the MXCC stream data registers
+
+The MXCC (the SuperSPARC's cache controller, on TI-SuperSparc-51, -61
+and -II) has a stream data register of 32 bytes at 0x01c00000 in ASI 2:
+four doublewords, which a stream source operation fills from memory and
+a stream destination operation writes out. QEMU took stores to them and
+used them for the stream operations, but read them as 0 ("unimplemented
+address").
+
+Sun's SPARCserver 600MP boot PROM writes walking ones to each doubleword
+from 0x01c00000 to 0x01c00038 and reads it back in its MXCC registers
+test, and loops on the first mismatch. Return the registers on a
+doubleword load, and take 0x01c00020-0x01c00038 as the same four
+registers again (Linux's asm/mxcc.h gives the stream size as 32 bytes;
+the PROM writes and reads back one address at a time, so it doesn't see
+whether those addresses alias). Only on the models with an MXCC
+(mxcc_version set); the others read 0 as before. No new state.
+
+With this and the store buffer registers the PROM passes its MXCC
+registers test on the default TI-SuperSparc-II.
