diff --git a/debian/patches/wsh/0160-hw-sparc-sun4m-report-SS-600MP-SBus-store-errors-as.patch b/debian/patches/wsh/0160-hw-sparc-sun4m-report-SS-600MP-SBus-store-errors-as.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3d70143
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/wsh/0160-hw-sparc-sun4m-report-SS-600MP-SBus-store-errors-as.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,197 @@
+From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
+Subject: [PATCH] hw/sparc/sun4m: report SS-600MP SBus store errors as M-to-S
+ write errors
+
+After the loads of its lance register size check, Sun's SPARCserver
+600MP boot PROM stores a byte, a word and a doubleword at the same
+offsets of the lance's page and wants each to come back as an
+asynchronous write error: a level 15 interrupt (trap 0x1f) and, in the
+IOMMU's M-to-S AFSR and AFAR at 0xf.e000_1000, the error and SBus
+error-acknowledge bits, the transaction size, supervisor mode, the
+CPU's module ID, address bits 4-0, the SBus transfer size and physical
+address bits 35-32 (SunOS's async.h, MTSAFSR_*), and the address bits
+31-0. For a byte store at 0xe.f006_0001 from CPU 0 that is 0x9180120e.
+
+New function sun4m_iommu_cpu_write_error() fills them and raises the
+IOMMU's interrupt; a second error before the AFSR is cleared only sets
+the multiple error bit. The SS-600MP (hwdef field sbus_bus_errors)
+sets the CPU feature buserr-trap and points the CPUs' store_error hook
+at it for physical addresses 0xe.xxxx_xxxx (the SBus); the other
+machines are unchanged. The IOMMU's interrupt stays on system interrupt
+bit 30, where QEMU has it; on the board the M-to-S write error is bit
+29. No new state.
+
+The PROM then passes the lance register size checks (progress 0xc1),
+0xc2 passes or is skipped, and it stops at 0xc3, the DMA control
+register.
+---
+ hw/sparc/sun4m.c               | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
+ hw/sparc/sun4m_iommu.c         | 43 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
+ hw/sparc/trace-events          |  1 +
+ include/hw/sparc/sun4m_iommu.h |  3 +++
+ 4 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/hw/sparc/sun4m.c b/hw/sparc/sun4m.c
